  <translations>
    <en>
      <description>Rain Bird 200-PEB is a professional 2″ solenoid valve for high-flow zones in parks, large gardens and commercial landscapes. Its glass-filled nylon body is designed for demanding irrigation installations, and the valve includes flow control and manual operation for servicing. Series specifications: operating pressure 1.4–13.8 bar; 24 VAC solenoid; flow should be determined by hydraulic design.</description>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>b0</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>b00</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <text>200-PEB</text>
        </children>
        <children>
          <_key>b01</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text> — a 2″ diaphragm solenoid valve for automatic irrigation.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h10</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Purpose and operating principle</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p1</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p10</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>The controller energises the solenoid, which operates the diaphragm and opens the water passage. When the signal stops, the valve closes automatically. The PEB series is intended for professional and commercial systems. Its glass-filled nylon body and reinforced diaphragm are designed for demanding service.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h20</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Construction and model-specific features</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p2</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p20</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>The reinforced body, flow control, internal manual operation and external bleed are designed for professional service. PEB is a professional series with a reinforced body, manual operation and slow-closing action.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h3</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h30</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Hydraulic and electrical specifications</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p3</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p30</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <marks>strong</marks>
          <text>Size 2″; operating pressure 1,4–13,8 bar; flow 75–200 GPM (17,03–45,40 m³/h); solenoid 24 VAC. Actual flow depends on pipe, filter and fitting losses as well as available pressure.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>h4</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>h40</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Installation, adjustment and maintenance</text>
        </children>
        <style>h2</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>p4</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>p40</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Connection: 2″ female NPT thread; BSP available by order. Before installation, confirm flow direction, operating pressure and thread standard. Fit the valve in an accessible valve box and flush the pipework before commissioning. During service, inspect the diaphragm, pilot filter, solenoid and seals. For flows below 1.14 m³/h, upstream filtration is recommended; below 2.27 m³/h, set the flow-control stem two full turns from fully open.</text>
        </children>
        <style>normal</style>
      </formattedDescription>
      <formattedDescription>
        <_key>l0</_key>
        <_type>block</_type>
        <children>
          <_key>l00</_key>
          <_type>span</_type>
          <text>Check flow direction and stay within the permitted operating pressure.</text>
        </children>
        <level>1</level>
